            <ArticleTitle>Ischemic stroke subtypes among Mexican Americans and non-Hispanic whites: the BASIC Project.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>574-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ischemic stroke subtype distribution was compared between Mexican Americans (MAs) and non-Hispanic whites (NHWs) in a community-based stroke surveillance study in Nueces County, TX. There was no difference in the distribution of stroke subtype by ethnicity (p = 0.19). There was a similar proportion of small-vessel and large-artery strokes between the two ethnic groups (p = 0.32). Differences in stroke rates among MAs and NHWs are not explained by the distribution of ischemic stroke subtypes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
